  <section|Closed in Chapter 6><label|closed-in-chapter-6>

  The first-power predictor proof now references ch04:predictor-comparison.

  The actual source is b_Y=b(V)+D_all(V)v_Y with clipped frozen displacement
  \|v_Y\|\<less\>=2d, d\<less\>=r t_f. Arbitrary frozen Haar logarithms are
  not small. Martin actual-global-row-prices.tex 300\U389 gives uniform
  base-row and all-coordinate derivative bounds. These yield actual
  forcing/mean O(t_f) and mean residual O(t_f exp(-cB)), with the original
  integrand preserved by correction factors.

  Actual-global-row-prices.tex 134\U298 gives actual replica-derivative gap
  and principal-window estimates from the common-tree comparison.
  Actual-local-compiler-handoff.tex 112\U196 gives anchored first/second
  derivatives and a common neighborhood with fixed selectors and preserved
  gap. General fixed order requires the corresponding higher path budget.

  Compensated-variation.tex supplies the global protected map: identity plus
  compactly supported log-composition perturbation with derivative norm
  \<less\>1/2, hence global bijection by contraction and smooth inverse.
  Exact link protection holds on the inner chart; strict nested supports give
  zero germs. Chapter now proves this construction.

  Gaussian-differentiation.tex 240 onward gives common finite-dimensional
  neighborhood domination for the density ratio. Neighborhood constants may
  depend on volume; basepoint derivatives have only polynomial dependence on
  region size. The covariance is the marginal covariance, not a principal
  block of full precision.

  Gaussian-moment-prices.tex and activity-jet-assembly.tex supply the added
  bounded-jet/common-law route. Actual protected pointwise jets and zero-germ
  cutoff support yield polynomial moments times square root of joint-event
  probability, without independence. The aggregate quadratic criterion
  remains an alternative, not an asserted necessary input.

  <section|Exact remaining warning compatibility><label|exact-remaining-warning-compatibility>

  Local-mean.tex 14\U79 cancels every linear row using full diagonalization
  AND stack identities. Summed quadratic matching alone is insufficient.
  Lines150\U174 use transported cut flat rows A_R^V;
  actual-local-compiler-handoff.tex55\U62 instead uses actual replica
  derivatives. Required transfer:

  \|\|(D_actual-D_transported)v_candidate\|\| \<less\>= C B^a t_f^2,

  in one common gauge, with candidate size \<less\>=C B^a t_f and identical
  guide, forest, frozen source and selected rows. Smooth Taylor/path
  estimates give this order once the constructions are identified. Chapter
  states the distinction and exact identity m-v=(AP-I)^<em|v-P^>(Av+f).
  Targets \<gtr\>30B from selected sites have their windows within one clean
  8B ball, inactive candidate coordinates vanish, and small affine candidate
  residual transfers to actual window mean.

  Warning-safety.tex140\U238 combines nonlinear affine error, noise response,
  and affine-mean residual. Half-size noise event leaves strict margins and
  zero germs. Actual-palette-warning.tex additionally compares actual and
  calibrated means (error \<less\>=x^-3/4), with explicit guide margins
  C/L\<twosuperior\>\<less\>=sqrt(c_direct)/64 and
  C+sqrt(c_direct)/64\<less\>=W sqrt(penalty)/4. All these same-guide
  identities have not yet been matched. Actual mask implication is not marked
  discharged.

  <section|Activity sums and auxiliary torus><label|activity-sums-and-auxiliary-torus>

  Actual pointwise amplitudes, both endpoint protections of quadratic
  itineraries, and full healthy neighborhoods for component extensions still
  require matching. Actual-harvested-owner-energy.tex, packet-estimates.tex,
  remote-action-jets.tex and activity-jet-assembly.tex are suppliers; scalar
  energy and common integration alone do not prove weighted sums of
  individual activities.

  Stationary-exterior-receipt.tex172\U190 assumes allocated pure expansion
  supported on fine toll\<less\>=tau/2, e_empty=1 and absolute nonempty
  sum\<less\>=exp(epsilon)-1. Its overhead Omega exp(-beta a_coarse,2 -logdet
  A0/2) is not merely sector Gaussian C_Y. Need exact allocation/determinant
  normalization and negative-exponent rooted activities before improved
  remainder. Parent investigates direct deterministic stationary-curvature
  route avoiding expansion/slack.

  <section|Validation><label|validation>

  Environment balance and reference resolution checked. No global build. No
  new bibliography keys. Foundations has now supplied ch5 actual
  geometry/gap; integrate its labels after checking selected row identity.

  <section|Subsequent closure in this task><label|subsequent-closure-in-this-task>

  Earlier remaining warning compatibility is superseded by
  ch06:mean-cancellation. Exact flat identities and quadratic matching give
  T<em|p=w, T>T+N*N=I and \|\|p\|\|\<twosuperior\>=\|\|w\|\|\<twosuperior\>,
  hence \|\|p\<minus\>Tw\|\|\<twosuperior\>=\<minus\>\|\|Nw\|\|\<twosuperior\>.
  Thus every row cancels and Nw=0; no extra null identity is assumed. One
  common gauge and the actual-derivative Taylor comparison transfer this to
  O(poly(B)t\<twosuperior\>) actual residual; the exact window identity
  supplies actual mean cancellation. Strict pre-L guide margins and half-size
  noise event give remote cutoff zero germs. The aligned full incoming
  quadratic/path identities remain explicit necessary hypotheses.

  Added ch06:primitive-bounds: exact inverse/determinant words, individually
  labelled itineraries, bounded-step counting, full halo cover weights and
  derivative polynomial costs. Ratio exp(-cB)poly(B) pays supports and gives
  any power x^-A. Source: itinerary-prices.tex full.

  The short-family table gives poly(B) times beta t\<threesuperior\>, beta
  t\<#2074\>, t, t\<twosuperior\>, incoming delta, t\<twosuperior\>Lambda,
  beta(t\<threesuperior\>+t\<#2074\>), beta t\<twosuperior\>exp(-cR).
  Positive support reserve is necessary for inherited conversion. Sources
  inherited-activity-prices.tex1\U150 and
  actual-corrected-body-compiler.tex100\U198. Derivatives use original smooth
  protected factors, NOT corrected compiler's merely continuous clamping.

  Component estimate uses energy reserve, subpower normalization/tag/frozen
  costs per selected test, annular cubic errors and finite-range selection
  counting. Review priority: exact row allocation matching.
  Gaussian-reassembly.tex108\U170 specifies near action/mean rows200B,
  determinants200B, Haar304B, component halo\<gtr\>=500B. These sets must not
  be unified. Chapter explicitly separates exact reconstruction from analytic
  bounds under this allocation.

  Added ch06:linear-comparison: same forest/windows on a clean local region
  gives covariance difference O(poly(B)t), mean difference
  O(poly(B)t\<twosuperior\>)+tails. Gaussian-unit shift is O(poly(B)g
  Mcut\<twosuperior\>). Physical map error
  O(poly(B)(t\<twosuperior\>+g\<twosuperior\>\|z\|\<twosuperior\>)),
  normalized by t gives t+g\<twosuperior\>/t with Gaussian moments. Positive
  covariance interpolation yields score gain x^-1/2+o(1). No comparison
  between different selectors or tree/smooth-gauge responses is asserted.

  Revalidated: references resolve, environments balanced, 8529 whitespace
  words. No global build.

  <section|Component extraction correction after independent
  review><label|component-extraction-correction-after-independent-review>

  Foundations correctly identified that core energy alone does not bound the
  extracted component: selected affine squares are subtracted in the near
  annulus. Replaced that argument with ch06:annulus-extraction and
  ch06:component-extracted-energy. Source
  actual-harvested-owner-energy.tex112\U252, packet-annulus.tex200\U355.

  The formula is signed average of E_core+W_annulus\<minus\>X_actual_selected+C(mean),
  with C nonnegative. Nonzero304B interfaces bound actual active coordinates;
  clean annular tree comparison puts frozen logs in their inner clipping
  plateau, so the SAME active/frozen/tree-zero signal reconstructs the
  physical field. Action rows200B, core2B, actualselectedH, separation205B,
  dependence500B, determinant200B andHaar304B are distinguished explicitly.

  Difference of nonlinear and actual-affine rows is
  E=poly(B)t\<twosuperior\>+tail, row norm M=poly(B)t. Half-square error
  \<less\>=E(2M+E)/2. Unselected residual squares are nonnegative; coarse
  counterterm/quartic defect and signed mismatch costs total
  poly(B)t\<threesuperior\>+poly(B)t\<twosuperior\>exp(-cR) per
  bounded-density row. Hence W\<minus\>X\<gtr\>=\<minus\>o(t\<twosuperior\>)n,
  and only THEN the core reserve bounds extracted energy. No positive
  uncontrolled Gaussian quadratic is dropped. X uses D times ACTIVE signal
  plus b_Y, with frozen contribution included exactly once.

  Review requested from foundations. No global build.

  <section|Final independent-review geometry and normalization
  fixes><label|final-independent-review-geometry-and-normalization-fixes>

  Applied all three follow-ups:

  <\enumerate>
    <item>Component estimate now explicitly requires the allocation's weak
    conditions through300B (unselected fine chord\<less\>=t_f/2, unselected
    mismatch\<less\>=2Wt_f, correct actual coarse flags absent off selected
    sites, positive retained frame likelihood). This is explicitly stronger
    than the opening5B consistency condition. Together with retained304B
    chart cutoffs it supplies the actual annular read hypotheses.

    <item>Ownership components merge intersecting closed500B neighborhoods;
    distinct owner halos are disjoint, separation\<gtr\>1000B sufficient.
    Removed misleading205B pairwise separation. This prevents
    duplicate200B/304B assignments without asserting independence. The
    enlarged finite-range adjacency changes only polynomial counting
    constants.

    <item>Annular X_H uses raw single-orientation rows D_sigma,b_sigma
    excluding sqrt(omega_sigma). Global precision stacks
    sqrt(omega_sigma)D_sigma. The extracted energy averages raw orientation
    energies exactly once, preventing squared orientation weights. Frozen
    source appears once via D_sigma times active signal plus b_sigma.
    Selected-stencil clearance now explicitly follows activecoordinate
    outside10B and stencilradius\<less\>=B/50, rather than
    annularanchor\<gtr\>2B alone.
  </enumerate>

  Renamed extracted component energy mathcal E_O^rem (mathcal H reserved for
  Hilbert spaces). Replaced component \Pinterface\Q wording by retained
  cutoff support; defined guides as the specified transported linear
  comparison rows. Prior unresolved-review statements above are historical
  and superseded by these fixes.
